## Coding Rules

Always:
- TypeScript strict mode
- reusable components
- no duplicated logic
- separate UI from business logic
- use server components first
- client components only when required
- no hardcoded secrets
- environment variables only
- keep files under 200 lines when possible

---

## UI Rules

Design must be:
- clean
- simple
- fast
- mobile first
- accessible

Avoid:
- unnecessary animations
- overengineering
- complex state management

---
## Testing Rules

Do not use strict TDD.

Development priority:
1. ship working features first
2. test critical business logic only

Must test:
- form validation
- Stripe webhook
- Supabase registration creation
- admin authentication
- CSV export

Preferred tools:
- Vitest for unit tests
- Playwright for end-to-end tests

Do not overtest UI styling.

## Performance Rules

Prefer:
- server components
- lazy loading
- optimized images
- minimal dependencies

---

## Security Rules

Always:
- protect admin routes
- use Supabase auth middleware
- validate all inputs
- use Row Level Security
- sanitize user input
- validate Stripe webhook signatures

---

## Final Rule

Priority order:
1. ship fast
2. keep code simple
3. keep architecture clean
4. prepare for future scale

MVP first.